<title>USA: TABLE - Moore Medical Q2 oper shr flat.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Moore Medical Q2 oper shr flat.</headline>
<dateline>NEW BRITAIN, Conn. 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second quarter	 Six months</p>
<p>				  1997	   1996     1997     1996</p>
<p> Net Sales		  $77,038     $72,840 $158,080 $148,673</p>
<p> Cost of products sold   65,687	62,058  135,513  127,294</p>
<p> Gross profit		11,351	10,782   22,567   21,379</p>
<p>Selling, general &amp;</p>
<p>administrative expenses</p>
<p>				  9,833	 9,284   19,797   18,442</p>
<p> Unusual item		   580	   ---	800	---</p>
<p> Operating Income	     938	 1,498    1,970    2,937</p>
<p> Interest expense, net	522	   513    1,039	979</p>
<p>Income before income taxes</p>
<p>				    416	   985	931    1,958</p>
<p> Income tax provision	 150	   344	335	684</p>
<p> Net Income		     266	   641	596    1,274</p>
<p> Net Income Per Share	 .09	   .22	.20	.44</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding</p>
<p>				  2,931	 2,918    2,925    2,914</p>
<p>NOTES: Full company name is Moore Medical Corp.</p>
<p>Periods ended June 28 vs June 29.</p>
<p>Excluding the $0.13 per share charge for exiting the government supply contract business, Q2 oper earings were flat with a year ago at $0.22 per share.</p>
<p>The charge associated with the business line exit was $0.18 per share for the first half.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
